AltoConvexCreditLineMarket::claimRewards()
├── given caller permissions and market state
│   ├── when caller is any unrelated account
│   │   └── it should remain permissionless
│   ├── when market is paused or frozen
│   │   └── it should remain available
│   └── when Convex strategy is inactive after emergency exit
│       └── it should remain available
├── given Convex reward claim
│   ├── it should call getReward for the market with claimExtras true
│   ├── when getReward reverts
│   │   └── it should propagate the failure without forwarding balances
│   └── when getReward returns false
│       └── it should revert with AltoConvexCreditLineExternalCallFailed
├── given configured reward token balances
│   ├── when every balance is zero
│   │   ├── it should perform no token transfers
│   │   ├── it should emit RewardsClaimed with zero for every token
│   │   └── it should return a zero amount for every token index
│   ├── when balances are nonzero
│   │   ├── it should forward each token's entire post-claim market balance
│   │   ├── it should include balances held before the Convex claim
│   │   ├── it should preserve configured token iteration order
│   │   ├── it should emit one RewardsClaimed event per token
│   │   └── it should return amounts aligned with rewardToken indexes
│   └── when all MAX_REWARD_TOKENS are configured
│       └── it should process each token exactly once in configured order
├── given rewards for an unconfigured token
│   └── it should leave that token in the market and exclude it from returned amounts and events
├── given a token removed before the claim
│   └── it should leave any newly distributed balance of that token in the market
└── given a successful claim
    ├── it should use the current rewardRecipient
    ├── it should not change reward configuration
    ├── it should not change credit collateral debt or supply accounting
    └── it should not change convexActive or staked collateral accounting
